  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.7.0: Long context, model validation, and state references\n- Added opt-in Request.LongContextEnabled and chainable EnableLongContext(), sending TypeSafe-Danger-Zone-Long-Context: true for that request only. Disabled by default; context beyond the default 64 KB is slower and less accurate. Enable only when needed.\n- Added Request.StrictValidation, default false. Unknown model identifiers and Box questions with jev-1.13.0 log a warning and proceed; strict mode throws InvalidOperationException before HTTP. The bundled known-version list may lag the API and does not replace API validation.\n- Added JevVersions constants and Versions list, plus JevModel.IsLatest, IsPreview, IsKnownVersion, and IsVersion inspection helpers.\n- Added request inspection helpers HasBoxQuestion and HasImages.\n- Automatic model selection now always uses JevModel.Latest, including Box questions. Explicit models remain unchanged; Box questions require jev-1.14.0 or later.\n- Added StateReference and StatePath, plus FormattableString instruction support with automatic backtick quoting through FormattableString.Escaped. Ordinary arguments retain their formatting.\n- Added AssetState.ToStateJson(), combining derived public readable properties and dictionary entries, honoring JSON property naming and ignore attributes, and rejecting duplicate JSON member names.\n- Fixed derived AssetState properties being omitted from request JSON, including asset state items in combined JevMessage content.\n- AssetState.AddAsset and GetRequiredImageAsset now accept StateReference. Strings remain usable through implicit conversion, but empty names, whitespace, and backticks are rejected. StatePath applies the same text validation; neither type verifies that a state field exists.",
